cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ABC: calibration-grade neural likelihoods for evidence accumulation models"
message: "If you use this software or its artefacts, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Heathcote
    given-names: Andrew
    affiliation: "University of Amsterdam"
  - family-names: Wuth
    given-names: Julian
repository-code: "https://github.com/ampl-psych/ABC"
license: GPL-3.0
abstract: >-
  Methods and diagnostics for building neural likelihood approximations of
  evidence accumulation models that are calibrated, not merely accurate
  pointwise. Includes the score-bias diagnostic and its analytic control, a
  simulation-based calibration harness, and validated flow artefacts for the
  DDM and RDM usable from EMC2.
keywords:
  - simulation-based inference
  - neural likelihood estimation
  - normalizing flows
  - simulation-based calibration
  - evidence accumulation models
  - diffusion decision model
